  + [decision] is implement a separate pure-first Rust crate with optional llama.cpp transport
  + [reason] is this keeps the conceptual experiment reversible prevents provider behavior from becoming host authority and gives every acceptance gate a cheap deterministic oracle
  + [alternative] is extend cantor_reflection_loop directly
  + [rejection_reason] is that crate proves a different route-attention reflection contract and mixing both experiments would weaken responsibility locality
  + [alternative] is modify llama.cpp or hidden attention state
  + [rejection_reason] is unnecessary for observable order-varied prompt projection and excluded by the source boundary
  + [counterargument] is four prompts from one model are correlated rather than independent observations
  + [answer] is the prototype claims order-stability only and requires explicit delineation while preserving the correlated-probe limitation
  + [confidence] is high for deterministic host contracts and moderate for useful small-model live behavior
  + [invalidation_condition] is the pure host cannot distinguish invalid identity or boundary behavior or the provider cannot produce inspectable closed output

